&lt;p&gt;Scopely is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Development Director - QA&lt;/strong&gt; located in our Barcelona studio to lead an ambitious, multi-faceted and continuously growing QA Program across Scopely’s portfolio of titles.The successful candidate will own the execution, growth for the initiatives part of QA programs for our projects around the globe and with each game team and development partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The QA Director&amp;nbsp; will partner in collaborating and coordinating with peers and senior management to ensure operations are aligned with the company mission, values, and long-term strategic goals as well as ensuring continued service improvements are implemented throughout the world on behalf of Scopely QA &amp;amp; Deployment. &lt;br&gt;It is a key position with high expectations on driving high impacts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The QA Director will help shape the future on how we continue to iterate and evolve our QA operations in deep partnership with game teams, to achieve high levels of execution efficiency while ensuring our products delight our users release after release though high quality of the player experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a key leader in an ambitious and continuously growing QA Program involving multiple disciplines, including Functionality QA, Dev QA and LiveOps QA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the evolution of a centralized DevQA program to support high quality game development on multiple platforms, across internal and external teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and champion QA best practices across the full development lifecycle, from concept to live Ops, enabling a shift left testing culture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong internal and ex-dev QA workflows, ensuring that all content developed meets internal quality standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership, technical expertise and career development for multiple QA Leaders, each of which are responsible for their own specific projects; support the growth of the discipline, leading to higher value individual contributors and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build on existing team metrics for measurement of quality and operational excellence and a consistent, regular process for assessment and improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build successful working relationships with external developer counterparts with a focus on Dev QA collaboration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be forward thinking and actively explore AI-driven QA solutions and emerging technologies to incorporate to the existing processes in order to future proof release quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain strong communication with cross-functional teams across all disciplines for both internal and external development and QA partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually improve the operational efficiency and effectiveness of the QA effort by assessing current practices and incorporating new strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an internal advocate and spokesperson for all things QA, specially as it relates to DevQA. Clearly communicate issues, risks, concerns, and successes to stakeholders about current production/QA workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold fellow leaders accountable for including quality as an essential factor in product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to performance evaluations of individuals and teams, compiling objective feedback that is channeled toward both personal and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for process Improvement; ownership of defining new processes and refining old processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9 + years quality assurance professional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 + years management experience in leading QA teams and groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading DevQA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience of working within a development game team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building a QA and DevQA organization that is responsible for end-to-end validation for a critical system or application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep ability to influence change that achieves exceptional product quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of cross platform and multiplatform titles (mobile, PC, Consoles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on AAA titles&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with remote teams and working with a cross functional team that is distributed around the globe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep cultural awareness and ability to work with varied teams across the globe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written/verbal communication in English, planning, implementation, project/ people management, time management, analytical and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and ease in interfacing with Senior Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and ability to multitask under pressure of hard deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of software testing, software QA processes, software development processes, change management and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence those not directly in your reporting structure, working to develop and maintain strong, effective relationships across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development (SDLC) practices &amp;amp; nomenclature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of quality assurance techniques, frameworks and methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and dynamic – quickly adapt to changing needs of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business awareness - the ability to view situations from a business perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong meeting organization and facilitation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that!&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state, and local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will have access to sensitive and/or confidential employee or customer personally identifiable information (PII) and/or Company financial information, and therefore will be subject to background checks upon receiving a conditional offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Niantic games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

greycroft-scopely:greenhouse:5162315008.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a LiveOps Specialist to join our MONOPOLY GO! This is a hybrid role based in Seville.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MONOPOLY GO! is a global phenomenon and the biggest mobile game launch in history, captivating millions of players worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a LiveOps Specialist, you will be joining a growing LiveOps team, where you will help to deliver a top-class user experience through targeted campaigns. You will own the execution of the LiveOps events and offers, be responsible for campaign validation through QA to ensure error-free release and closely work with other teams across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute LiveOps campaigns using bespoke in-house tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other teams to test functionality pre-release to ensure error-free execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the live events and investigate any issues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer communication channels (in-app messages &amp;amp; push notifications) using relevant segmentation for maximum impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the AB testing setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve processes and raise tool or feature improvement requests.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on tasks and projects with teams based in Spain and the United States - including Production, QA, Art and Economy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have good communication skills, a strong sense of prioritisation, be able to manage multiple projects at the same time and work in a dynamic environment. We are looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in working with a wide range of stakeholders, from QA to analytics to art to product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own, build and iterate functions and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactivity in identifying risks and making changes when necessary with an appropriate sense of urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving skills and an ability to apply logical thinking to encountered issues to find workarounds when necessary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-centric approach and passion for improving the player experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with focus on delivering results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good technical skills and ability to use high complexity tools or programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in games, particularly mobile games is a plus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creativity. You’ll have to make the leap from understanding what’s going on to brainstorming ways to improve it. Ultimately, success is about implementing campaigns and events that have a big impact on our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Previous experience in QA, programming or IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Niantic games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

greycroft-scopely:greenhouse:5195469008.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Niantic (now Scopely), the creator of hit games including Pokémon GO, Pikmin Bloom, Monster Hunter Now, and&amp;nbsp; is seeking a General Manager to lead the Monster Hunter Now franchise.&amp;nbsp; You will lead a talented, fast paced, multi-disciplinary team of game makers based in Tokyo, with supporting team members in San Francisco, Culver City and Seattle. You will be responsible for driving the end to end game vision, franchise strategy, and ultimately business results.&amp;nbsp; Your role will be central in living up to the ambitious vision for Monster Hunter Now, inspiring millions of players to get out, go hunt, and grow stronger together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the game leadership team, developing leaders across disciplines including Design, Product, Production, and Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a franchise strategy that delivers strong business results across a multi-year time horizon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive rigor across the product development process, actively engaging in the roadmap, production pipeline, and live ops calendar development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drive the adoption of AI to accelerate productivity, leading from the front by building and utilizing on a daily basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Product Reviews, providing feedback and coaching to ensure excellent, mission aligned product design for all features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take accountability for driving KPI impact via a well executed Product, Live Ops and Data strategy &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive market analysis, user research, and knowledge sharing across the team to drive more effective decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong, collaborative relationship with IP holders, ensuring brand integrity and generating concepts (both in game and marketing) that resonate with fans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deeply integrated audience strategy working across both Product and Marketing to drive player growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Monster Hunter Now team and franchise in executive forums with leadership from across Niantic and Scopely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft and execute a thoughtful AI strategy to augment the performance of both the team and the game using forward looking technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional team members and stakeholders, including regular and reliable attendance and leadership of key meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a driver of culture on the team, fostering learning, collaboration, player centricity, and excellence with an outcome oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required in-office 3 days per week on Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years leadership experience in free to play gaming, with hands on experience in Product, Design and/or Production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of operating and scaling successful free to play mobile games post-launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing roadmaps and shipping KPI impacting features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of content development and live operations in midcore games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management experience across creative and analytical disciplines including Product, Design, Live Operations and Production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with analyzing and interpreting data to make data informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication in both English and Japanese&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort partnering with and influencing executive stakeholders across time zones and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage, coach, and lead by example to develop team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility in a demanding team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for video games; an avid gamer with a proven understanding of mobile games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked in a leadership role on a high profile game with a significant amount of daily active users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced hybrid environment and handle stress appropriately and ability to solve practical problems and be sufficiently adaptable to handle dynamic situations with little advance notice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on cross-functional teams with ability to communicate effectively through written and verbal communications, including asynchronous interactions with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Belief in the value of bringing people together through games to explore in the real world&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in, or able to relocate and work in Japan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plus If...!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Deep understanding and/or fandom of the Monster Hunter franchise&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Familiarity as a player with Monster Hunter Now, Pikmin Bloom, and/or Pokemon Go&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience, interest, and excitement around AR/location based games or features&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
